-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Third-party material: not covered by this licence
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The model carries codes, and in places names and translations, from external
code systems. Those remain the property of their owners and are used under
their owners' terms. Neither licence above grants any right in them.

- LOINC. This material contains content from LOINC (http://loinc.org). LOINC is
  copyright © Regenstrief Institute, Inc. and the Logical Observation
  Identifiers Names and Codes (LOINC) Committee and is available at no cost
  under the license at http://loinc.org/license. LOINC® is a registered
  United States trademark of Regenstrief Institute, Inc.

- SNOMED CT. This material includes SNOMED Clinical Terms® (SNOMED CT®)
  which is used by permission of SNOMED International (the International
  Health Terminology Standards Development Organisation). All rights
  reserved. SNOMED CT® was originally created by the College of American
  Pathologists. "SNOMED" and "SNOMED CT" are registered trademarks of SNOMED
  International. This covers the identifiers, their display terms, and the
  labels and translations derived from them, including the CH Term value sets
  and the concepts of the Swiss extension published by eHealth Suisse, the
  Swiss National Release Centre. Health Data Safe holds a SNOMED CT Affiliate
  Licence, obtained through eHealth Suisse. Health Data Safe grants you no
  licence or sublicence in SNOMED CT: to use it you need your own licence,
  which is free of charge in member territories (Switzerland is one) through
  the National Release Centre, and may carry fees elsewhere. See
  https://www.snomed.org/get-snomed.

- Other code systems named in the definitions (ICD-10, ICD-10-PCS, ICF,
  RxNorm, CPT, Swissmedic, HL7 terminology, HGNC, HGVS, dbSNP, ClinVar, UCUM,
  and others) are referenced under their publishers' terms. CPT is a
  proprietary code system of the American Medical Association.

- Names of third-party methods, products and applications (for example
  fertility-awareness methods and tracking apps in the converter definitions)
  are used for identification only and remain their owners' trademarks.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Notice on the model's name and on conformance
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This section adds no condition to the licences above. It states how Health
Data Safe uses the model's name, and recalls what CC BY 4.0 already provides.

You may fork, adapt and redistribute the model, including in commercial or
closed products, and you may describe a product as "compatible with the HDS
Data Model <version>" when it reads and writes data as that published version
defines.

Health Data Safe alone publishes the HDS Data Model and defines what conforms
to it. A modified version is not the HDS Data Model. CC BY 4.0 requires you to
indicate that you modified it (section 3(a)(1)(B)), and gives no permission to
suggest that Health Data Safe endorses you or your version (section
2(a)(6)). CC BY 4.0 does not license trademark or name rights (section
2(b)(2)); Health Data Safe reserves its rights in the names "Health Data
Safe", "HDS" and "HDS Data Model" under applicable law. Health Data Safe may
also ask you to remove its attribution from a modified version (section
3(a)(3)). Please do not name a modified version "HDS Data Model", or present
it as an official or conformant version.
